module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.ConormalModuleBaseChangeEpi
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.UniversalThickeningFunctorial

/-!
# The universal first-order thickening of a composition of algebraic spaces

Let `Z ⟶ Y ⟶ X` be morphisms of algebraic spaces over a scheme `S`, let `Z ⊂ Z'` be a universal
first-order thickening of `Z` over `X` with structure morphism `pZ : Z' ⟶ X`, and let `Y ⊂ Y'`
be a universal first-order thickening of `Y` over `X` with structure morphism `pY : Y' ⟶ X`.
Stacks 06BF constructs a morphism `h : Z' ⟶ Y'` and asserts that `Y ×_{Y'} Z'` is the universal
first-order thickening of `Z` over `Y`, and that there is a canonical exact sequence

```
  i^*𝒞_{Y/X} ⟶ 𝒞_{Z/X} ⟶ 𝒞_{Z/Y} ⟶ 0
```

whose maps are those of Stacks 060A, where `i : Z ⟶ Y` is the first of the two morphisms.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.universalThickeningCompMap`: **Stacks 06BF, clause (1)**, the
  morphism `h : Z' ⟶ Y'`.  It is the canonical morphism of Stacks 060A for the square with
  `g = 𝟙 X`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.universalThickeningCompFibre`: the fibre product `Y ×_{Y'} Z'`,
  realized as the closed subspace `h⁻¹(Y)` of `Z'`, together with its structure morphism
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.universalThickeningCompStructure` to `Y` and the copy
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.universalThickeningCompSub` of `Z` inside it.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.universalThickeningCompMap_restrict` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.universalThickeningCompMap_over_hom`: the morphism `h` restricts to
  `i` on `Z` and satisfies `h ≫ pY = pZ`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isUniversalFirstOrderThickening_comp`: **Stacks 06BF, clause (1)**,
  `Y ×_{Y'} Z'` is a universal first-order thickening of `Z` over `Y`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.epi_conormalMap_comp`: **Stacks 06BF, clause (2), at the right
  term**: the canonical map `𝒞_{Z/X} ⟶ 𝒞_{Z/Y}` of Stacks 04CP is surjective.

## Implementation notes

**The fibre product is a closed subspace of `Z'`.**  The inclusion `Y.ι` is a monomorphism, so
`Y ×_{Y'} Z'` is the inverse image `h⁻¹(Y)`, a closed subspace of `Z'` by Stacks 083Q.  Taking
it in that form is what makes the right-hand map of clause (2) an instance of the
surjectivity clause of Stacks 04CQ (`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.epi_conormalMap`), which is stated
for the inverse-image configuration.

**`Z` inside the fibre product is taken as an inverse image too.**  This development has no
composition of closed subspaces, so the copy of `Z` inside `Y ×_{Y'} Z'` is the inverse image of
`Z ⊆ Z'` along the inclusion of `Y ×_{Y'} Z'`.  This is the same convention as
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.epi_conormalMap_closedSubspaces`.

**Formal unramifiedness is not a hypothesis.**  The source assumes `Z ⟶ Y` and `Y ⟶ X` formally
unramified and then speaks of *the* universal first-order thickenings, whose existence is
Stacks 0606, a tag this library does not carry; so the two thickenings are hypotheses, exactly
as in `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Spaces/UniversalThickeningFunctorial.lean`.  That `Z ⟶ X`
factors through `Y ⟶ X` is the hypothesis `hfac` below, which is the only use the source makes
of the datum `Z ⟶ Y ⟶ X`.

**The square-zero condition inside the fibre product is a hypothesis.**  That the copy of `Z`
is a *first-order* thickening of `Y ×_{Y'} Z'` is a base-change statement of the kind of part
(2) of Stacks 09ZX, which this library carries only along an étale morphism: the defining ideal
of an inverse image is known to be generated by the pulled-back ideal only on affine charts
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.definingIdealAt_preimage_eq_map`), for want of the quasi-coherence of
Stacks 03MB.  See the implementation notes of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Spaces/Thickenings/BaseChange.lean`.  Accordingly
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isUniversalFirstOrderThickening_comp` takes that condition as a
hypothesis; the universal lifting property, which is the content of the clause, is proved.

## What is not proved

* **Exactness in the middle of clause (2) of Stacks 06BF is not proved**, and nothing here
  carries that part of the tag.  The left-hand map `i^*𝒞_{Y/X} ⟶ 𝒞_{Z/X}` of the sequence is
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.universalThickeningConormalMap` applied to the square of
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.universalThickeningComp_square`, so it exists; what is missing is the
  exactness.  The source deduces it from Stacks 06BD, whose exactness in the middle is not
  formalized at the level of algebraic spaces nor at the scheme level
  (`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Conormal/ConormalSequence.lean` carries only
  `@[stacks 062S "exactness at the right term: the canonical map 𝒞_{Z/X} ⟶ 𝒞_{Z/Y} is epi"]`),
  and from the flat clause of Stacks 04CQ, which is not formalized either.  Only exactness at
  the right term is proved here.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 06BF](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/06BF)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 060A](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/060A)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0602](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0602)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 04CP](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04CP)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 04CQ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04CQ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 06BD](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/06BD)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 083Q](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/083Q)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 09ZX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09ZX)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits
open Stacks.Thickenings

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Space

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)
    {X Y' Z' : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS} {Y : Subfunctor Y'.obj} {Z : Subfunctor Z'.obj}
    {pY : Y' ⟶ X} {pZ : Z' ⟶ X} (i : Z.toFunctor ⟶ Y.toFunctor)
    (hZ : IsUniversalFirstOrderThickening B S hS Z pZ)
    (hY : IsUniversalFirstOrderThickening B S hS Y pY)
    (hfac : Z.ι ≫ pZ.hom = i ≫ Y.ι ≫ pY.hom)

/-! ### The lifting property of a fibre product of universal first-order thickenings -/

include hZ in
/-- The universal lifting property of the fibre product, in the form in which both clause (1)
of Stacks 06BF and its proof use it.  Let `Z ⊂ Z'` and `Y ⊂ Y'` be universal first-order
thickenings over `X`, let `h : Z' ⟶ Y'` restrict to `i : Z ⟶ Y` and lie over `X`, and let
`π : P ⟶ Y` exhibit `P` as the fibre product `Y ×_{Y'} Z'`, with second projection `κ` a
monomorphism.  Then `Z ×_{Z'} P ⊂ P` is a universal first-order thickening of `Z` over `Y`.

A morphism `T' ⟶ P` is a pair of morphisms to `Y` and to `Z'` agreeing over `Y'`.  The morphism
`e : T' ⟶ Z'` is the unique one furnished by the universal property of `Z ⊂ Z'` over `X`; that
`e ≫ h` agrees with the given `T' ⟶ Y ⟶ Y'` is uniqueness in the universal property of
`Y ⊂ Y'`, since both restrict to `Z ⟶ Y` on `T` and lie over `X`. -/
private theorem isUniversalFirstOrderThickening_of_isPullback
    (h : Z' ⟶ Y') (hres : Z.ι ≫ h.hom = i ≫ Y.ι) (hover : h.hom ≫ pY.hom = pZ.hom)
    {P : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS}
    (π : P ⟶ (⟨Y.toFunctor, (IsNthOrderThickening.isThickening B S hS hY.firstOrder).1.1⟩ :
      AlgebraicSpaces B S hS))
    {κ : P.obj ⟶ Z'.obj} (hpb : IsPullback π.hom κ Y.ι h.hom) (hmono : Mono κ)
    (hfirst : IsFirstOrderThickening B S hS P (Z.preimage κ)) :
    IsUniversalFirstOrderThickening B S hS (Z.preimage κ) π := by
  have := hmono
  have hπι : π.hom ≫ Y.ι = κ ≫ h.hom := hpb.w
  have hζι : Z.fromPreimage κ ≫ Z.ι = (Z.preimage κ).ι ≫ κ := Subfunctor.fromPreimage_ι Z κ
  refine ⟨hfirst, ?_⟩
  intro T' T hT a b hcompat
  have hb : T.ι ≫ b ≫ Y.ι = ((a ≫ Z.fromPreimage κ) ≫ i) ≫ Y.ι := by
    rw [← Category.assoc, hcompat]
    simp only [Category.assoc]
    rw [hπι, ← Category.assoc ((Z.preimage κ).ι), ← hζι]
    simp only [Category.assoc]
    rw [hres]
  have hcompatY : T.ι ≫ b ≫ Y.ι ≫ pY.hom =
      ((a ≫ Z.fromPreimage κ) ≫ i) ≫ Y.ι ≫ pY.hom := by
    simpa only [Category.assoc] using congrArg (fun t => t ≫ pY.hom) hb
  -- Push the solid diagram into `Z'` and lift it by universality of `Z ⊂ Z'` over `X`.
  have hcompatZ : T.ι ≫ b ≫ Y.ι ≫ pY.hom = (a ≫ Z.fromPreimage κ) ≫ Z.ι ≫ pZ.hom := by
    rw [hcompatY, Category.assoc, ← Category.assoc i, ← hres]
    simp only [Category.assoc, hover]
  obtain ⟨e, he, heu⟩ := hZ.existsUnique_lift T hT (a ≫ Z.fromPreimage κ)
    (b ≫ Y.ι ≫ pY.hom) hcompatZ
  -- The two morphisms `T' ⟶ Y'` agree, by uniqueness in the universal property of `Y ⊂ Y'`.
  obtain ⟨y₀, -, hyu⟩ := hY.existsUnique_lift T hT ((a ≫ Z.fromPreimage κ) ≫ i)
    (b ≫ Y.ι ≫ pY.hom) hcompatY
  have hagree : b ≫ Y.ι = e ≫ h.hom := by
    refine (hyu (b ≫ Y.ι) ⟨hb, by simp only [Category.assoc]⟩).trans
      (hyu (e ≫ h.hom) ⟨?_, ?_⟩).symm
    · rw [← Category.assoc, he.1]
      simp only [Category.assoc]
      rw [hres]
    · rw [Category.assoc, hover]
      exact he.2
  -- Assemble the lift from the mapping property of the fibre product.
  refine ⟨hpb.lift b e hagree, ⟨?_, hpb.lift_fst b e hagree⟩, ?_⟩
  · refine (cancel_mono κ).mp ?_
    rw [Category.assoc, hpb.lift_snd, he.1]
    simp only [Category.assoc]
    rw [hζι]
  · intro c hc
    refine (cancel_mono κ).mp ?_
    rw [hpb.lift_snd]
    refine heu (c ≫ κ) ⟨?_, ?_⟩
    · rw [← Category.assoc, hc.1]
      simp only [Category.assoc]
      rw [← hζι]
    · rw [Category.assoc, ← hover, ← Category.assoc κ, ← hπι]
      simp only [Category.assoc]
      rw [← Category.assoc c π.hom, hc.2]

include hfac

/-! ### The morphism between the two universal first-order thickenings -/

/-- The factorization `Z ⟶ Y ⟶ X` of the structure morphism of `Z`, written as the
commutative square of Stacks 060A with `g = 𝟙 X`. -/
theorem universalThickeningComp_square :
    Z.ι ≫ pZ.hom ≫ (𝟙 X : X ⟶ X).hom = i ≫ Y.ι ≫ pY.hom := by
  rw [show (𝟙 X : X ⟶ X).hom = 𝟙 X.obj from rfl, Category.comp_id]
  exact hfac

/-- **Stacks 06BF, clause (1), the morphism `Z' ⟶ Y'`.**  Let `Z ⊂ Z'` be a universal
first-order thickening of `Z` over `X` and let `Y ⊂ Y'` be a universal first-order thickening of
`Y` over `X`, and let the structure morphism of `Z` factor through `Y`.  The morphism
`h : Z' ⟶ Y'` is the canonical morphism of Stacks 060A for the square with `g = 𝟙 X`, that is
the unique morphism restricting to `i : Z ⟶ Y` and lying over `X`. -/
@[stacks 06BF "clause (1): the morphism Z' ⟶ Y'"]
noncomputable def universalThickeningCompMap : Z' ⟶ Y' :=
  universalThickeningMap B S hS (𝟙 X : X ⟶ X) i hZ hY
    (universalThickeningComp_square B S hS i hfac)

/-- The morphism `h : Z' ⟶ Y'` restricts to `i : Z ⟶ Y`. -/
theorem universalThickeningCompMap_restrict :
    Z.ι ≫ (universalThickeningCompMap B S hS i hZ hY hfac).hom = i ≫ Y.ι :=
  universalThickeningMap_restrict B S hS (𝟙 X : X ⟶ X) i hZ hY
    (universalThickeningComp_square B S hS i hfac)

/-- The morphism `h : Z' ⟶ Y'` lies over `X`: composing it with the structure morphism of `Y'`
gives the structure morphism of `Z'`. -/
theorem universalThickeningCompMap_over_hom :
    (universalThickeningCompMap B S hS i hZ hY hfac).hom ≫ pY.hom = pZ.hom := by
  have h := universalThickeningMap_over B S hS (𝟙 X : X ⟶ X) i hZ hY
    (universalThickeningComp_square B S hS i hfac)
  rw [Category.comp_id] at h
  exact congrArg (fun k : Z' ⟶ X => k.hom) h

/-! ### The fibre product `Y ×_{Y'} Z'` -/

/-- The fibre product `Y ×_{Y'} Z'`, as a closed subspace of `Z'`: the inclusion of `Y` is a
monomorphism, so the fibre product is the inverse image `h⁻¹(Y)`, which is a closed subspace by
Stacks 083Q. -/
noncomputable abbrev universalThickeningCompFibreSubspace : ClosedSubspaces B S hS Z'.obj :=
  ⟨Y.preimage (universalThickeningCompMap B S hS i hZ hY hfac).hom,
    isClosedSubspace_preimage B S hS
      (universalThickeningCompMap B S hS i hZ hY hfac).hom Y Y'.2 Z'.2
      (IsNthOrderThickening.isThickening B S hS hY.firstOrder).1⟩

/-- The fibre product `Y ×_{Y'} Z'`, as an algebraic space over `S`. -/
noncomputable abbrev universalThickeningCompFibre : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS :=
  ⟨(universalThickeningCompFibreSubspace B S hS i hZ hY hfac).1.toFunctor,
    (universalThickeningCompFibreSubspace B S hS i hZ hY hfac).2.1⟩

/-- The inclusion `Y ×_{Y'} Z' ⟶ Z'`. -/
noncomputable abbrev universalThickeningCompFibreInclusion :
    universalThickeningCompFibre B S hS i hZ hY hfac ⟶ Z' :=
  subspaceInclusion B S hS Z' (universalThickeningCompFibreSubspace B S hS i hZ hY hfac)

/-- The structure morphism `Y ×_{Y'} Z' ⟶ Y`, the projection to the first factor. -/
noncomputable abbrev universalThickeningCompStructure :
    universalThickeningCompFibre B S hS i hZ hY hfac ⟶
      (⟨Y.toFunctor, (IsNthOrderThickening.isThickening B S hS hY.firstOrder).1.1⟩ :
        AlgebraicSpaces B S hS) :=
  ObjectProperty.homMk
    (Y.fromPreimage (universalThickeningCompMap B S hS i hZ hY hfac).hom)

/-- The copy of `Z` inside the fibre product `Y ×_{Y'} Z'`: the inverse image of `Z ⊆ Z'` along
the inclusion of the fibre product. -/
noncomputable abbrev universalThickeningCompSub :
    Subfunctor (universalThickeningCompFibre B S hS i hZ hY hfac).obj :=
  Z.preimage (universalThickeningCompFibreSubspace B S hS i hZ hY hfac).1.ι

/-! ### Clause (1): the fibre product is the universal first-order thickening over `Y` -/

/-- **Stacks 06BF, clause (1), the universal first-order thickening of `Z` over `Y`.**  With the
morphism `h : Z' ⟶ Y'` of `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.universalThickeningCompMap`, the fibre
product `Y ×_{Y'} Z'` is a universal first-order thickening of `Z` over `Y`, with structure
morphism the projection to `Y`.

A morphism `T' ⟶ Y ×_{Y'} Z'` is a pair of morphisms to `Y` and to `Z'` agreeing over `Y'`.
Given a solid diagram over `Y` built from a first-order thickening `T ⊂ T'` and a morphism
`T ⟶ Z`, the morphism to `Y` is the one the diagram supplies and the morphism `e : T' ⟶ Z'` is
the unique one furnished by the universal property of `Z ⊂ Z'` over `X`.  That the two agree
over `Y'` is uniqueness in the universal property of `Y ⊂ Y'`: both composites restrict to
`Z ⟶ Y` on `T` and lie over `X`, the first because `h` restricts to `i` and lies over `X`.
Uniqueness of the resulting morphism is uniqueness of `e` together with the fact that the
inclusion of the fibre product into `Z'` is a monomorphism.

That the copy of `Z` is a first-order thickening of `Y ×_{Y'} Z'` is a hypothesis; see the
implementation notes of this file. -/
@[stacks 06BF "clause (1): Y ×_{Y'} Z' is the universal first-order thickening of Z over Y, \
the square-zero condition inside the fibre product being hypothesised"]
theorem isUniversalFirstOrderThickening_comp
    (hfirst : IsFirstOrderThickening B S hS
      (universalThickeningCompFibre B S hS i hZ hY hfac)
      (universalThickeningCompSub B S hS i hZ hY hfac)) :
    IsUniversalFirstOrderThickening B S hS
      (universalThickeningCompSub B S hS i hZ hY hfac)
      (universalThickeningCompStructure B S hS i hZ hY hfac) :=
  isUniversalFirstOrderThickening_of_isPullback B S hS i hZ hY
    (universalThickeningCompMap B S hS i hZ hY hfac)
    (universalThickeningCompMap_restrict B S hS i hZ hY hfac)
    (universalThickeningCompMap_over_hom B S hS i hZ hY hfac)
    (universalThickeningCompStructure B S hS i hZ hY hfac)
    (Subfunctor.isPullback_preimage
      (universalThickeningCompMap B S hS i hZ hY hfac).hom Y)
    inferInstance hfirst

/-! ### Clause (2): exactness at the right term -/

/-- **Stacks 06BF, clause (2), at the right term.**  The canonical map
`𝒞_{Z/X} ⟶ 𝒞_{Z/Y}` of Stacks 04CP — the right-hand map of the conormal sequence of the
composition — is surjective.

By Stacks 0607 the conormal module of a formally unramified morphism is the conormal module of
its source inside its universal first-order thickening, so `𝒞_{Z/X}` is the conormal module of
`Z` in `Z'` and, by clause (1), `𝒞_{Z/Y}` is the conormal module of the copy of `Z` inside
`Y ×_{Y'} Z'`.  The map between them is the one of Stacks 04CP for the inclusion
`Y ×_{Y'} Z' ⟶ Z'`, and surjectivity is the surjectivity clause of Stacks 04CQ,
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.epi_conormalMap`, for that inverse-image configuration.

The left-hand map of the sequence is `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.universalThickeningConormalMap`
for the square of `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.universalThickeningComp_square`; exactness in the
middle is not proved, see the "What is not proved" section of this file. -/
@[stacks 06BF "clause (2): exactness at the right term, the canonical map 𝒞_{Z/X} ⟶ 𝒞_{Z/Y} \
being surjective"]
theorem epi_conormalMap_comp :
    Epi (conormalMap B S hS
      (preimageSubspace B S hS
        (universalThickeningCompFibreInclusion B S hS i hZ hY hfac)
        ⟨Z, (IsNthOrderThickening.isThickening B S hS hZ.firstOrder).1⟩)
      ⟨Z, (IsNthOrderThickening.isThickening B S hS hZ.firstOrder).1⟩
      (universalThickeningCompFibreInclusion B S hS i hZ hY hfac)
      (preimageProjection B S hS
        (universalThickeningCompFibreInclusion B S hS i hZ hY hfac)
        ⟨Z, (IsNthOrderThickening.isThickening B S hS hZ.firstOrder).1⟩)
      (conormalEtaleRestrictionSquare B S hS
        (universalThickeningCompFibreInclusion B S hS i hZ hY hfac)
        ⟨Z, (IsNthOrderThickening.isThickening B S hS hZ.firstOrder).1⟩)) :=
  epi_conormalMap B S hS (universalThickeningCompFibreInclusion B S hS i hZ hY hfac)
    ⟨Z, (IsNthOrderThickening.isThickening B S hS hZ.firstOrder).1⟩

end AlgebraicGeometry.Space

end
